          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;â€œYouâ€™ve been kinda quietâ€¦â€ Adora observes, her voice soft and concerned. Catra doesnâ€™t say anything for a moment before she shrugs a bit.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œIâ€™m fine, just...thinking a lot. If we get into this school, we have to leave everything behind. Itâ€™s scary,â€ She tells her, letting go of Adoraâ€™s hand so she can shove them in her own pockets.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adora shifts away, looking worried. â€œI know. Itâ€™ll be hard. Butâ€¦â€ She sighs. â€œYou donâ€™t have to do this Catra,â€ She reminds her.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Catra shakes her head quickly. â€œNo, Iâ€™m doing this. Youâ€™re not getting rid of me that easy,â€ She teases with a grin, nudging her with her elbow. Adora laughs, pressing a kiss to her cheek.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œGood.â€&lt;br /&gt;Â &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;***&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adora and Catra have big dreams of a life, a career, and a future together up on Broadway, up on that stage. But what happens when only Adora is presented with the opportunity to pursue her dreams?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;What happens when she's forced to make a decision that will change every plan they'd ever made together..?&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
